Braces enclose the statements in a function, branch or loop. A function names its parameters between pipes. Call it with arguments in parentheses.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    greet |name String| {
        io.line([: Hello, [name]!])
    }

    greet("Priya")
]

Here `name` is the function's parameter. The brackets construct a String from text and the value of `name`. The closing brace ends the function.

A Boolean decision uses one pair of braces. A bare `else` starts the other branch inside those braces.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    if ready {
        io.line("Ready!")
    else
        io.line("Waiting")
    }
]

Each branch has its own scope. A name you declare in the first branch is visible only there. Indentation helps you see the nesting. The braces and branch headers mark the boundaries.
